{"cells":[{"source":"<a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/code/kimbengfranklingent/google-project-capstone-mets-values?scriptVersionId=286923641\" target=\"_blank\"><img align=\"left\" alt=\"Kaggle\" title=\"Open in Kaggle\" src=\"https://kaggle.com/static/images/open-in-kaggle.svg\"></a>","metadata":{},"cell_type":"markdown"},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"06d4cac6","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.006212,"end_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:42.272101","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:42.265889","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["---\n","# Google Capstone Project: using MET- Minutes to track volume of physical activity\n","### Marketing Strategy for Bellabeat Global - Spring product (Analysis based on Fitbit tracker data)\n","##### Franklin-Gent, Nango Kimbeng\n","###### **Date: 2022-05-14**\n","---"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"1bd4a9f5","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.004896,"end_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:42.282087","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:42.277191","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Introduction\n","\n","Bellabeat uses the spring (water bottle) product by trackings daily water intake of it's customers to ensure they are appropriately hydrated. Understanding how people are already using their smart devices, could help inform Bellabeat's marketing strategy. After looking into activities (fibit steps tracked data), it was necessary to carry out further analysis regarding the METs values."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"b0fc2e79","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.004961,"end_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:42.292091","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:42.28713","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["#### Data Preparation with Google Bigquery\n","```sql\n","    \n","    -- Setting variables for time of day/ day of week analyses\n","DECLARE\n","\n"," MORNING_START,\n"," \n"," MORNING_END,\n"," \n"," AFTERNOON_END,\n"," \n"," EVENING_END INT64;\n"," \n"," -- Set the times for the times of the day\n"," \n","SET\n"," MORNING_START = 6;\n","SET\n"," MORNING_END = 12;\n","SET\n"," AFTERNOON_END = 18;\n","SET\n"," EVENING_END = 21;\n","\n","-- Creating an temporary table after cleaning time entries \n","-- and formating date entries\n","\n","WITH new_met AS (\n","\n","      SELECT\n","          Id,\n","        FORMAT_DATE('%Y-%m-%d', PARSE_DATE('%m/%d/%Y', activity_date)) \n","        AS mets_date,\n","        \n","        CASE \n","          WHEN Activity_time LIKE '%A' \n","            THEN CONCAT(SUBSTR(Activity_time,1,9),' ', 'AM')\n","          WHEN Activity_time LIKE '%P' \n","            THEN CONCAT(SUBSTR(Activity_time,1,9),' ', 'PM') \n","        \n","          ELSE\n","            Activity_time\n","        END AS \n","          activity_time,\n","\n","          METs\n","\n","      FROM\n","\n","        `arcane-dynamics-312220.dailyactivity.mets`\n",")\n","\n","SELECT\n","-- Managing given time into weekly categories such \n","-- as Weekdays and Time of the day\n","\n","    --FORMAT_TIMESTAMP('%w',mets_time) AS dow_number\n","    FORMAT_TIMESTAMP('%A', mets_time) AS day_of_week,\n","    CASE\n","     WHEN FORMAT_TIMESTAMP('%A',mets_time) IN \n","     (\"Sunday\", \"Saturday\") THEN \"Weekend\"\n","    ELSE\n","    \"Weekday\"\n","    END AS part_of_week,\n","\n","    CASE \n","      WHEN TIME(mets_time) BETWEEN TIME(MORNING_START, 0, 0) \n","      AND TIME(MORNING_END, 0, 0) THEN \"Morning\"\n","      WHEN TIME(mets_time) BETWEEN TIME(MORNING_END, 0, 0) \n","      AND TIME(AFTERNOON_END, 0, 0) THEN \"Afternoon\"\n","      WHEN TIME(mets_time) BETWEEN TIME(AFTERNOON_END, 0, 0) \n","      AND TIME(EVENING_END, 0, 0) THEN \"Evening\"\n","      WHEN TIME(mets_time) >= TIME(EVENING_END, 0, 0) \n","      OR \n","      TIME(TIMESTAMP_TRUNC(mets_time, Minute)) \n","      <= TIME(MORNING_START, 0, 0) THEN \"Night\"\n","\n","    ELSE\n","      \"ERROR\"\n","    END AS time_of_day,\n","\n","-- Approximate MET values for a variety of light, moderate, and vigorous \n","-- activities. See chart for comparism, \n","-- Source: https://www.healthline.com/health/what-are-mets#examples\n","    \n","-- Deriving the METs value From Minute-METs rounded up to 1dp\n","\n","    IF\n","      (\n","        EXTRACT(MINUTE FROM mets_time) > 0,\n","      ROUND(METs / EXTRACT(MINUTE FROM mets_time), 1), \n","      EXTRACT(MINUTE FROM mets_time)\n","      ) AS mets_pro_mins\n","\n","   --mets_time,\n","    -- METs\n","  \n","  FROM\n","    (\n","    SELECT\n","    \n","      Id,\n","      \n","      TIMESTAMP(CONCAT(mets_date,\" \",PARSE_TIME('%I:%M:%S %p', activity_time)))\n","      \n","      AS mets_time,\n","      \n","      METs\n","      \n","    FROM \n","     new_met\n","    )"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"7dd35078","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2025-12-17T22:20:42.30823Z","iopub.status.busy":"2025-12-17T22:20:42.305981Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-12-17T22:20:44.284225Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-12-17T22:20:44.28228Z"},"papermill":{"duration":1.987827,"end_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:44.287048","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:42.299221","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["── \u001b[1mAttaching packages\u001b[22m ─────────────────────────────────────── tidyverse 1.3.1 ──\n","\n","\u001b[32m✔\u001b[39m \u001b[34mggplot2\u001b[39m 3.3.5     \u001b[32m✔\u001b[39m \u001b[34mpurrr  \u001b[39m 0.3.4\n","\u001b[32m✔\u001b[39m \u001b[34mtibble \u001b[39m 3.1.6     \u001b[32m✔\u001b[39m \u001b[34mdplyr  \u001b[39m 1.0.8\n","\u001b[32m✔\u001b[39m \u001b[34mtidyr  \u001b[39m 1.2.0     \u001b[32m✔\u001b[39m \u001b[34mstringr\u001b[39m 1.4.0\n","\u001b[32m✔\u001b[39m \u001b[34mreadr  \u001b[39m 2.1.2     \u001b[32m✔\u001b[39m \u001b[34mforcats\u001b[39m 0.5.1\n","\n","── \u001b[1mConflicts\u001b[22m ────────────────────────────────────────── tidyverse_conflicts() ──\n","\u001b[31m✖\u001b[39m \u001b[34mdplyr\u001b[39m::\u001b[32mfilter()\u001b[39m masks \u001b[34mstats\u001b[39m::filter()\n","\u001b[31m✖\u001b[39m \u001b[34mdplyr\u001b[39m::\u001b[32mlag()\u001b[39m    masks \u001b[34mstats\u001b[39m::lag()\n","\n","\n","Attaching package: ‘lubridate’\n","\n","\n","The following objects are masked from ‘package:base’:\n","\n","    date, intersect, setdiff, union\n","\n","\n","\n","Attaching package: ‘janitor’\n","\n","\n","The following objects are masked from ‘package:stats’:\n","\n","    chisq.test, fisher.test\n","\n","\n","here() starts at /kaggle/working\n","\n","\n","Attaching package: ‘reshape2’\n","\n","\n","The following object is masked from ‘package:tidyr’:\n","\n","    smiths\n","\n","\n"]}],"source":["# Installing necessary packages for analysis\n","library(tidyverse)\n","library(ggplot2)\n","library(lubridate)\n","library(skimr)\n","library(janitor)\n","library(here)\n","library(reshape2)\n","library(dplyr)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":2,"id":"59aaadf5","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2025-12-17T22:20:44.334324Z","iopub.status.busy":"2025-12-17T22:20:44.30177Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-12-17T22:20:45.580013Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-12-17T22:20:45.577869Z"},"papermill":{"duration":1.288884,"end_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:45.583016","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:44.294132","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["\u001b[1mRows: \u001b[22m\u001b[34m1325580\u001b[39m \u001b[1mColumns: \u001b[22m\u001b[34m4\u001b[39m\n","\u001b[36m──\u001b[39m \u001b[1mColumn specification\u001b[22m \u001b[36m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\n","\u001b[1mDelimiter:\u001b[22m \",\"\n","\u001b[31mchr\u001b[39m (3): day_of_week, part_of_week, time_of_day\n","\u001b[32mdbl\u001b[39m (1): mets_pro_mins\n","\n","\u001b[36mℹ\u001b[39m Use `spec()` to retrieve the full column specification for this data.\n","\u001b[36mℹ\u001b[39m Specify the column types or set `show_col_types = FALSE` to quiet this message.\n"]}],"source":["# importing dataset for analysis\n","\n","\n","mets <- read_csv(\"../input/mets-analysis/met_analysis.csv\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":3,"id":"6c992d39","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2025-12-17T22:20:45.597942Z","iopub.status.busy":"2025-12-17T22:20:45.596361Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-12-17T22:20:45.628409Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-12-17T22:20:45.625319Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.059239,"end_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:45.648039","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:45.5888","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["spec_tbl_df [1,325,580 × 4] (S3: spec_tbl_df/tbl_df/tbl/data.frame)\n"," $ day_of_week  : chr [1:1325580] \"Tuesday\" \"Tuesday\" \"Tuesday\" \"Tuesday\" ...\n"," $ part_of_week : chr [1:1325580] \"Weekday\" \"Weekday\" \"Weekday\" \"Weekday\" ...\n"," $ time_of_day  : chr [1:1325580] \"Night\" \"Morning\" \"Evening\" \"Morning\" ...\n"," $ mets_pro_mins: num [1:1325580] 4 2.3 1.9 3 6.3 2.6 11.3 3.5 15 2.4 ...\n"," - attr(*, \"spec\")=\n","  .. cols(\n","  ..   day_of_week = \u001b[31mcol_character()\u001b[39m,\n","  ..   part_of_week = \u001b[31mcol_character()\u001b[39m,\n","  ..   time_of_day = \u001b[31mcol_character()\u001b[39m,\n","  ..   mets_pro_mins = \u001b[32mcol_double()\u001b[39m\n","  .. )\n"," - attr(*, \"problems\")=<externalptr> \n"]}],"source":["# Structure of the dataset\n","\n","str(mets)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":4,"id":"d20f1382","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2025-12-17T22:20:45.663842Z","iopub.status.busy":"2025-12-17T22:20:45.662254Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-12-17T22:20:45.692744Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-12-17T22:20:45.690369Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.041884,"end_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:45.696205","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:45.654321","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<table class=\"dataframe\">\n","<caption>A tibble: 6 × 4</caption>\n","<thead>\n","\t<tr><th scope=col>day_of_week</th><th scope=col>part_of_week</th><th scope=col>time_of_day</th><th scope=col>mets_pro_mins</th></tr>\n","\t<tr><th scope=col>&lt;chr&gt;</th><th scope=col>&lt;chr&gt;</th><th scope=col>&lt;chr&gt;</th><th scope=col>&lt;dbl&gt;</th></tr>\n","</thead>\n","<tbody>\n","\t<tr><td>Tuesday</td><td>Weekday</td><td>Night    </td><td>4.0</td></tr>\n","\t<tr><td>Tuesday</td><td>Weekday</td><td>Morning  </td><td>2.3</td></tr>\n","\t<tr><td>Tuesday</td><td>Weekday</td><td>Evening  </td><td>1.9</td></tr>\n","\t<tr><td>Tuesday</td><td>Weekday</td><td>Morning  </td><td>3.0</td></tr>\n","\t<tr><td>Tuesday</td><td>Weekday</td><td>Afternoon</td><td>6.3</td></tr>\n","\t<tr><td>Tuesday</td><td>Weekday</td><td>Night    </td><td>2.6</td></tr>\n","</tbody>\n","</table>\n"],"text/latex":["A tibble: 6 × 4\n","\\begin{tabular}{llll}\n"," day\\_of\\_week & part\\_of\\_week & time\\_of\\_day & mets\\_pro\\_mins\\\\\n"," <chr> & <chr> & <chr> & <dbl>\\\\\n","\\hline\n","\t Tuesday & Weekday & Night     & 4.0\\\\\n","\t Tuesday & Weekday & Morning   & 2.3\\\\\n","\t Tuesday & Weekday & Evening   & 1.9\\\\\n","\t Tuesday & Weekday & Morning   & 3.0\\\\\n","\t Tuesday & Weekday & Afternoon & 6.3\\\\\n","\t Tuesday & Weekday & Night     & 2.6\\\\\n","\\end{tabular}\n"],"text/markdown":["\n","A tibble: 6 × 4\n","\n","| day_of_week &lt;chr&gt; | part_of_week &lt;chr&gt; | time_of_day &lt;chr&gt; | mets_pro_mins &lt;dbl&gt; |\n","|---|---|---|---|\n","| Tuesday | Weekday | Night     | 4.0 |\n","| Tuesday | Weekday | Morning   | 2.3 |\n","| Tuesday | Weekday | Evening   | 1.9 |\n","| Tuesday | Weekday | Morning   | 3.0 |\n","| Tuesday | Weekday | Afternoon | 6.3 |\n","| Tuesday | Weekday | Night     | 2.6 |\n","\n"],"text/plain":["  day_of_week part_of_week time_of_day mets_pro_mins\n","1 Tuesday     Weekday      Night       4.0          \n","2 Tuesday     Weekday      Morning     2.3          \n","3 Tuesday     Weekday      Evening     1.9          \n","4 Tuesday     Weekday      Morning     3.0          \n","5 Tuesday     Weekday      Afternoon   6.3          \n","6 Tuesday     Weekday      Night       2.6          "]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["# A preview of the dataset\n","\n","head(mets)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"f6a8aad0","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.005973,"end_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:45.708305","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:45.702332","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["- **day_of_week**: Daily METs value\n","- **part_of_week**: Weekend: Saturday and Sunday or Weekdays: Mondays - Fridays\n","- **time_of_day**: Time of the day : Morning, Afternoon, Evening and Night of the measured value\n","- **mets_pro_mins**: Values derived from the Minute-METS \n","  -(see sql query above for metrics)\n","\n","**More on METs**: Physical activities may be rated using METs(Metabolic equivalents of task ) to indicate their intensity, **Source**: [Healthline.com](https://www.healthline.com/health/what-are-mets#examples).\n","\n","\n","#### **Sample chart representing approximate values for a variety of light, moderate and vigorous activities based on a person weighing 70kg or 154lbs**, Source: [Healthline.com](https://www.healthline.com/health/what-are-mets#examples)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"6df6dc58","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.005944,"end_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:45.720212","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:45.714268","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["\n",">To better understand the likely activities and its intensities, we begin by considering only non zero METs values. That is, days and times for which there is an indication of a certain kind of activity.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":5,"id":"f6f85865","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2025-12-17T22:20:45.736829Z","iopub.status.busy":"2025-12-17T22:20:45.734837Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-12-17T22:20:46.638796Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-12-17T22:20:46.637119Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.916111,"end_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:46.642412","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:45.726301","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# Data Preparation\n","# Approximate MET values for a variety of light, moderate, \n","# and vigorous activities. See chart above for comparism.\n","\n","count_n <- mets %>% \n","# Categorising the METs values into light, moderate and vigorous activity\n","  mutate(activity_intensity = case_when(mets_pro_mins < 3 ~ 'light', mets_pro_mins  >= 3 & mets_pro_mins <= 6 ~ 'moderate', mets_pro_mins > 6  ~ 'vigorous', TRUE ~ 'other')) %>%\n","select(day_of_week, time_of_day, mets_pro_mins, activity_intensity) %>%\n","# neglecting states of no activity\n","filter(mets_pro_mins == 0) %>% \n","group_by(day_of_week, time_of_day) %>%\n","count(mets_pro_mins) %>%\n","arrange(-n)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":6,"id":"4dc473ba","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2025-12-17T22:20:46.658002Z","iopub.status.busy":"2025-12-17T22:20:46.65642Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-12-17T22:20:46.687438Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-12-17T22:20:46.685204Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.04214,"end_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:46.690675","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:46.648535","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<table class=\"dataframe\">\n","<caption>A grouped_df: 6 × 4</caption>\n","<thead>\n","\t<tr><th scope=col>day_of_week</th><th scope=col>time_of_day</th><th scope=col>mets_pro_mins</th><th scope=col>n</th></tr>\n","\t<tr><th scope=col>&lt;chr&gt;</th><th scope=col>&lt;chr&gt;</th><th scope=col>&lt;dbl&gt;</th><th scope=col>&lt;int&gt;</th></tr>\n","</thead>\n","<tbody>\n","\t<tr><td>Tuesday  </td><td>Night  </td><td>0</td><td>1201</td></tr>\n","\t<tr><td>Wednesday</td><td>Night  </td><td>0</td><td>1185</td></tr>\n","\t<tr><td>Thursday </td><td>Night  </td><td>0</td><td