tivity_count) + \n","  geom_bar(aes(x = activity_intensity, y = n, fill = activity_intensity), stat=\"identity\", position = \"dodge\", width = 0.7) + \n","  geom_text(aes(x = activity_intensity, y = n, label = n), colour = \"white\", size = 3, vjust = 1.5, position = position_dodge(.9)) + \n","  \n","# changing the legends title with guides\n","  guides(fill=guide_legend(title=\"Intensity\")) +\n","  \n","  labs(title=\"Volume of physical activity\", caption=paste0(\"DataSource: FitBit Fitness Tracker Data (CC0: Public Domain, datasets made available through **Mobius** on Kaggle)\"), x = \"Activity Intensity\", y = \"Count\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"e0e4c89f","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.00794,"end_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:48.303036","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:48.295096","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["#### Daily physical activity analysis\n","\n","- The analysis on steps showed higher activites on Tuesdays, Wednesdays and Thursdays than the rest of weekdays\n","see [Average Daily Fitbit Activity (steps)](https://www.kaggle.com/code/kimbengfranklingent/google-project-capstone)\n","- Generally, these activities are light in intensity, such as strolling at very slow pace and have same trend as the [Average Daily Fitbit Activity (steps)](https://www.kaggle.com/code/kimbengfranklingent/google-project-capstone) analysis.\n","- Tuesdays records a higher activity in all intensities; light, medium and vigorous.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":12,"id":"66737019","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2025-12-17T22:20:48.32398Z","iopub.status.busy":"2025-12-17T22:20:48.322437Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-12-17T22:20:49.039009Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-12-17T22:20:49.037245Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.731056,"end_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:49.041604","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:48.310548","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# Data Preparation\n","\n","dow_intensity <- mets %>% \n","# Approximate MET values for a variety of light, moderate, and vigorous activities. See chart above for comparism.\n","mutate(activity_intensity = case_when(mets_pro_mins < 3 ~ 'light', mets_pro_mins  >= 3 & mets_pro_mins <= 6 ~ 'moderate', mets_pro_mins > 6  ~ 'vigorous', TRUE ~ 'other')) %>%\n","select(day_of_week, mets_pro_mins, activity_intensity) %>%\n","filter(mets_pro_mins > 0) %>%\n","group_by(day_of_week, activity_intensity) %>%\n","count(activity_intensity) %>%\n","arrange(-n)\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":13,"id":"7af45bd6","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2025-12-17T22:20:49.0593Z","iopub.status.busy":"2025-12-17T22:20:49.057565Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-12-17T22:20:49.088295Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-12-17T22:20:49.085919Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.043297,"end_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:49.091923","exception":false,"start_time":"2025-12-17T22:20:49.048626","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<table class=\"dataframe\">\n","<caption>A grouped_df: 6 × 3</caption>\n","<thead>\n","\t<tr><th scope=col>day_of_week</th><th scope=col>activity_intensity</th><th scope=col>n</th></tr>\n","\t<tr><th scope=col>&lt;chr&gt;</th><th scope=col>&lt;chr&gt;</th><th scope=col>&lt;int&gt;</th></tr>\n","</thead>\n","<tbody>\n","\t<tr><td>Tuesday  </td><td>light</td><td>195831</td></tr>\n","\t<tr><td>Wednesday</td><td>light</td><td>193198</td></tr>\n","\t<tr><td>Thursday </td><td>light</td><td>178367</td></tr>\n","\t<tr><td>Friday   </td><td>light</td><td>162985</td></tr>\n","\t<tr><td>Saturday </td><td>light</td><td>158329</td></tr>\n","\t<tr><td>Sunday   </td><td>light</td><td>158051</td></tr>\n","</tbody>\n","</table>\n"],"text/latex":["A grouped\\_df: 6 × 3\n","\\begin{tabular}{lll}\n"," day\\_of\\_week & activity\\_intensity & n\\\\\n"," <chr> & <chr> & <int>\\\\\n","\\hline\n","\t Tuesday   & light & 195831\\\\\n","\t Wednesday & light & 193198\\\\\n","\t Thursday  & light & 178367\\\\\